  <layout>Running head top left, page number top right. One page of text: first a block of verse in four-line stanzas, a horizontal rule, then a title "CALENDÆ MAIÆ." and a verse stanza below it. No margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>77</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Non enim moles Pariæ columnæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Phidiæ aut vivax ebur, aut Myronis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Æra, mansuræ poterunt sacrare</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Nomina famæ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Obruet longos cita mors labores,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Obruet claros titulos, opésque,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Saxa findentur vitiata serae</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Dente senectæ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Mulciber quamuis &amp; iniqua Juno</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Verterint urbem Priami superbam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Illa Smyrnæis inimica pensat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Fata Camœnis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Nec suo mallet cineri superstes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Ilium Eois dare jura terris,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Quà patent fuscos Rhodope ab nivosa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Usque sub Indos.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Sola doctorum monumenta vatum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Nesciunt fati imperium severi,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Sola contemnunt Phlegetonta, &amp; Orci</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Jura severa.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" type="heading" level="2" para="true">CALENDÆ MAIÆ.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>SAluete festis deliciis sacræ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Maia calendæ, lætitiæ &amp; mero</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Ludisque dicatæ jocisque,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Et teneris Charitum choreis.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>No margin notes. Right margin shows faint show-through from the reverse page, not transcribed. The initial S of "Saluete" is a large decorative initial and is joined to its word. The first stanza's opening is a continuation from the previous page only in layout; the verse itself starts here, so cont="true" is applied to the first stanza as a fragment of the preceding poem.</notes>
</page>
